<header>
  <div class="eyebrow">DeepSeek Harness · Daliesk</div>
  <h1>Proving Ground</h1>
  <p class="lede">Every recorded run of the bench on the operator's subscription, folded from the session logs on disk: what certified, at which attempt, at what cost, and which comparisons hold above the bench's own noise.</p>
  <div class="stats" id="stats"></div>
</header>
<main>
  <section id="live-section" hidden>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Running now</h2><p>Folded from the run directory's session logs at build time; a run in flight has no verdict yet.</p></div>
    <div class="verdicts" id="live"></div>
  </section>
  <section>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Verdicts</h2><p>Each card is one paired comparison: certificates per arm, the paired delta with its bootstrap interval, and the verdict rule read on that interval. Frozen pairs ran as one experiment; offline folds pair two separately recorded runs.</p></div>
    <div class="toggles" id="verdict-filters"></div>
    <div class="verdicts" id="verdicts"></div>
  </section>
  <div class="two">
    <section class="panel">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>Product models on sealed tier 5</h2><p>Plain single-model arms on the harness loop over the eight audited tasks, two repetitions at seed 2, three attempts; every sealed run of the same arm is pooled.</p></div>
      <div id="models"></div>
    </section>
    <section class="panel">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>Cost of a certificate</h2><p>Output tokens spent per certificate earned: each arm's output tokens over all its cells, divided by the certificates it produced.</p></div>
      <div id="cost"></div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <section class="panel">
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Difficulty matrix</h2><p>Certification rate per environment and route over sealed runs; a cell reads certified of run. Routes are the first rung, then the ladder, then the implementer.</p></div>
    <div class="toggles" id="matrix-toggles"></div>
    <div class="matrix-wrap" id="matrix"></div>
  </section>
  <section class="panel timeline">
    <div class="section-head"><h2>When it ran</h2><p>Each bar is one record from its first session to its last, by kind. Click a bar to open the record below.</p></div>
    <div id="timeline"></div>
  </section>
  <section>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Records</h2><p>One row per recorded run; click a row for its cells and its README paragraph.</p></div>
    <div class="controls" id="record-controls"></div>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="records" id="records"></table></div>
  </section>
  <div class="two">
    <section class="panel">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>Routing, read offline</h2><p>Over the three single-model arms at seed 2: an oracle picks the cheapest certifying model per cell; a cascade tries the models in order and pays every stage.</p></div>
      <div id="routing"></div>
    </section>
    <section class="panel">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>Noise floor</h2><p>Run-to-run agreement of one arm on the same sixteen cells. A paired delta inside one arm's own flip rate says nothing.</p></div>
      <div id="repeatability"></div>
    </section>
  </section>
  <section class="panel" id="dataset-section" hidden>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Training corpus</h2><p id="dataset-lede"></p></div>
    <div class="two" id="dataset"></div>
  </section>
  <section class="panel">
    <div class="section-head"><h2>How to read this page</h2></div>
    <div class="notes" id="notes"></div>
  </section>
</main>
